{
  "id": "O5",
  "appendix": "G",
  "description": "The store pair check (1.6.1): input.myshopify_domain is the v3 snapshot's, input.merchant_origin its storefront origin, and input.response what GET expected.url answered (no cookies, credentials, Authorization or buyer data; redirects never followed; expected.url null: no request is made). A response with pad_to_bytes has its body padded with trailing spaces to that many bytes (the bytes read). expected.reason names the failing rule, in the order the checks run: not_https, bad_origin, not_public, bad_domain, redirect, status, content_type, too_large, not_json (invalid, a BOM, empty, or a duplicate member name), not_object, missing, not_string, non_ascii, differs. A network error or a timeout is a failure too. The check runs before the completing report, so a failure is local: nothing is reported and the buyer can still hand off. A failure is never cached.",
  "limits": {
    "timeout_seconds": 5,
    "max_body_bytes": 65536,
    "cache_ttl_seconds_max": 86400
  },
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "match",
      "input": {
        "merchant_origin": "https://shop.example",
        "myshopify_domain": "test-shop.myshopify.com",
        "response": {
          "status": 200,
          "content_type": "application/json; charset=utf-8",
          "body": "{\"name\":\"Test Shop\",\"myshopify_domain\":\"test-shop.myshopify.com\"}"
        }
      },
      "expected": {
        "url": "https://shop.example/meta.json",
        "valid": true,
        "reason": null
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "match, application/json without parameters",
      "input": {
        "merchant_origin": "https://shop.example",
        "myshopify_domain": "test-shop.myshopify.com",
